# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# ---
# COMMIT MESSAGE TEMPLATE FOR YUKTA
#
# TYPE: feat, fix, docs, test, refactor, chore, style, perf, ci, build
#
# SCOPE (optional): The area affected by this change
#   Examples: cli, core, web, ui, plugin-api, mcp, messaging, boot, build-logic
#
# SUBJECT (required):
#   - Use imperative mood ("add" not "added" or "adds")
#   - Do not capitalize first letter
#   - Limit to 50 characters
#   - Do not end with period
#
# BODY (optional):
#   - Wrap at 72 characters
#   - Explain what and why, not how
#   - Separate paragraphs with blank lines
#
# FOOTER (optional):
#   - Reference issues: "Fixes #123", "Closes #456"
#   - Document breaking changes: "BREAKING CHANGE: ..."
#   - No Co-Authored-By lines (use git commit --co-authored-by in CI/bots only)
#
# EXAMPLES:
#
# feat(cli): add workflow status command
#
# Add a new status subcommand to fetch current workflow execution state
# with human-readable formatting. Connects to the ControlBus REST API
# and displays node progress, timestamps, and error details if present.
#
# Fixes #142
#
# ---
#
# fix(core): prevent race condition in plugin lifecycle
#
# Synchronize ActivePluginRegistry state transitions with a read-write lock
# to avoid stale-workflow cleanup interfering with concurrent executions.
# Adds unit tests covering concurrent registration and cleanup.
#
# Fixes #156
#
# ---
#
# build(deps): bump actions/checkout from 4 to 7 (#199)
#
# Automated dependency update via Dependabot. No manual changes.
#
